    <rich_text scale="h3">1. MODULE OBJECTIVE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The Database Module provides persistent storage for the SchemaX Student Information System.
It allows the application to connect to MySQL and manage student records and related academic information.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. DATABASE SETUP</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Name:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> schemax_sis
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Management System:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Management Tool:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL Workbench
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">SQL Setup File:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> db/schemax_sis.sql
The original database setup contains four primary application tables:
1. students — Stores student information.

2. subjects — Stores subject information.

3. student_subjects — Stores student enrollments and grades.

4. attendance — Stores attendance records.

The database uses relational tables to organize student and academic information.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. DATABASE CONNECTION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Source File:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Data/Db.cs
The Db class is responsible for opening MySQL database connections.
The application reads its connection string from appsettings.json.
The Db.Open() method creates and opens a MySQL connection.
Database credentials must remain private and should not be uploaded to GitHub.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. DATABASE REPOSITORY COMPONENTS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">StudentRepository.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Contains database operations for inserting, retrieving, updating, deleting, searching, and filtering student records.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">AcademicRepository.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Contains database operations for managing subjects, student enrollments, and grades.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">DashboardRepository.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Retrieves database statistics used by the application's dashboard.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">UserRepository.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Provides database operations for user registration and authentication.
These components are present in the integrated project. Their inclusion here documents the database module's interfaces with the rest of the application; it does not attribute every repository implementation to one developer.

</rich_text>
