    <rich_text scale="h3">6. OCTOBER 22 INTEGRATION UPDATE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The latest application required additional local database changes to support authentication and dashboard functionality.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Issue 1: Missing users Table</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The local database did not contain the users table required for registration and login.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Resolution:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> The required table was created locally.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Registration and login passed.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Issue 2: Missing students.user_id Column</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Dashboard queries required a user_id column that was absent from the original students table.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Resolution:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> The existing table was backed up, the column was added, and the two original student records were associated with the registered test account.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Dashboard statistics and student record retrieval passed.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> These local corrections must be reflected in the final database setup or migration scripts before deployment.

</rich_text>
