    <rich_text scale="h3">1. MODULE OBJECTIVE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The CRUD Module allows users to create, retrieve, update, and delete student records through the Student Information System.
It connects the Windows Forms interface to the MySQL database through the StudentRepository class.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. CREATE — ADD STUDENT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository Method:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> StudentRepository.Insert()
The Add Student feature validates the entered student information before attempting to save a new record.
The repository executes a parameterized SQL INSERT statement to store the student's information.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result — October 17: PASS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
A valid temporary student record was successfully saved to MySQL and displayed in the application.
The temporary record was removed after testing.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. READ — VIEW STUDENT RECORDS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository Methods:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
StudentRepository.GetAll()
StudentRepository.GetById()
The application retrieves student information from MySQL and displays existing records in the DataGridView.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result — October 17: PASS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Existing student records were successfully loaded and displayed.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. UPDATE — EDIT STUDENT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository Method:</rich_text>
