The Edit Student feature allows the user to select an existing student, modify information, and save the changes.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result — October 17: PASS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
An existing student's block was modified and saved successfully.
The updated value was verified in MySQL, and the original value was restored after testing.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">5. DELETE — REMOVE STUDENT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository Method:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> StudentRepository.Delete()
The Delete Student feature allows the user to remove an existing record after confirmation.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result — October 17: PASS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
A confirmed deletion successfully removed the selected student record.
Canceling deletion preserved the record.
Deleting without selecting a student displayed the appropriate warning.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">6. SEARCH AND FILTERING INTEGRATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository Method:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> StudentRepository.Search()
The application supports searching and filtering student records.
Verified scenarios included:
• Student ID searching

• Student name searching

• Partial matching

• Case-insensitive searching

• Year Level filtering

• Program filtering

• Combined search and filtering


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result — October 17: PASS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application displayed matching student records as expected.
Search and filtering are included here as related student-management integration features, not as exclusively Mariane's assigned work.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">7. INPUT VALIDATION AND DUPLICATE HANDLING</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The CRUD interface uses validation checks before saving student information.
Tested scenarios included:
◇ Missing Student ID

◇ Invalid Student ID format

◇ Missing student name

◇ Invalid contact number

◇ Missing program

◇ Missing gender

◇ Missing year level

◇ Duplicate Student ID


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS for the recorded functional tests.
Duplicate BU email handling was also tested during subsequent integration work.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">8. IDENTIFIED BUG — EDIT MODE AFTER DELETION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Bug ID:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> BUG-007
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Date Identified:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> October 17, 2026
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> After deleting a student, the application could remain in Edit Mode.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Cause:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> The _isEdit state was not reset after deletion.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Correction Implemented:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Added ExitEditMode() to the deletion handler's finally block.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Build Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Final Regression Test:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PENDING
Immediate Add Mode behavior after deletion without using Clear Selection still requires verification.

</rich_text>
