    <rich_text scale="h2">4. BUG REPORTS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">BUG-01: Search Button Not Responding</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Severity:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Medium
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> OPEN — Pending Team Coordination
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Type:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> UI Functionality / Integration
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Steps to Reproduce:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open the Enrolled Students form.

2. Enter "John" in the Search field.

3. Click the Search button.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application should display matching student records or an appropriate no-results response.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Actual Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
No visible response occurs when the Search button is clicked.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Investigation Findings:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• The Search button's Click event field is blank in the Windows Forms Designer.

• The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">txtSearch_TextChanged()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> method exists but has an empty body.

• No </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">btnSearch</rich_text>
    <rich_text> reference was found in </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">studentForm.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Possible Cause:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The Search event handler or search functionality has not yet been implemented or connected.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Recommended Action:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Coordinate with the team to complete Search functionality and retest after integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">BUG-02: CRUD Database Integration Incomplete</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Severity:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> High
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> OPEN
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Type:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Database / CRUD Integration
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Investigation Findings:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">ADD:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Input validation is implemented.

◇ Valid student information is added to the DataGridView.

◇ The inspected </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">btnAdd_Click()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> method does not call the repository's </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Insert()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> method.

◇ Database persistence is not implemented in the inspected handler.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">EDIT:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ The no-selection validation is implemented.

◇ The inspected </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">btnEdit_Click()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> method contains no editing or database update logic after the selection check.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">DELETE:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ The no-selection validation is implemented.

◇ A confirmation dialog is displayed when a student is selected.

◇ The inspected </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">btnDelete_Click()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> method ends after checking the confirmation response.

◇ No actual deletion logic is implemented in the inspected handler.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">SEARCH:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Search functionality is documented separately under BUG-01.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">DATABASE REPOSITORY:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">StudentRepository.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text> contains the following methods:
▪ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Insert()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

▪ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">GetById()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

▪ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Update()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

▪ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Delete()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

▪ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">GetAll()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>



◇ These methods use </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Db.Open()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> to establish a MySQL connection.

◇ The inspected student form handlers do not call the repository methods.

◇ Successful database connectivity has not yet been verified.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
CRUD operations should save, retrieve, update, and delete student records in MySQL, with corresponding changes displayed in the user interface.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Actual Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The inspected student form handlers perform validation and limited UI operations but do not execute database CRUD operations.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Recommended Action:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Complete UI-to-repository integration and perform end-to-end database testing.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">BUG-03: Exception Handling Not Integrated</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Severity:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> High
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> OPEN
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Type:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Error Handling / Integration
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Investigation Findings:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Searched the entire Visual Studio solution using Find in Files.

◇ The search covered 19 files.

◇ No calls to </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExceptionHandler.Handle()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> were found.

◇ The only call to </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ErrorLog.LogError()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> was located in </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExceptionHandler.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

◇ The only </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">catch</rich_text>
    <rich_text> block found was also located in </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExceptionHandler.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

◇ No application-level exception-handling integration was identified in the searched source files.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Application operations should handle relevant exceptions, display user-friendly error messages, and record technical details in the error log.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Actual Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The error-handling utilities exist and have passed earlier tests, but integration into the application's operational code was not found.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Recommended Action:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Integrate exception handling into appropriate application operations and verify its behavior through end-to-end testing.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Integration Testing Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
PENDING — Requires completed application and database integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">5. ERROR LOGGING AND EXCEPTION HANDLING VERIFICATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Test:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Error Logging and Exception Handling
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
