    <rich_text family="monospace">errors.txt</rich_text>
    <rich_text> file exists inside the folder.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ErrorLogTest.RunTest()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> recorded a test exception on October 14, 2026.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExceptionHandlerTest.RunTest()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> recorded a test exception on October 14, 2026.

◇ Both entries contain:
▪ Date and time

▪ Exception type

▪ Exception message

▪ Stack trace



◇ Both test records are present in the same log file.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Conclusion:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Error logging successfully recorded the two previously executed test exceptions. The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExceptionHandler</rich_text>
    <rich_text> implementation also includes protection against failures during logging.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Limitation:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
These results verify test exception logging. Exception handling during actual CRUD and MySQL failures remains untested.


