    <rich_text weight="heavy">BUG-04: Application Remains in Edit Mode After Deletion</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Severity:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Medium
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> FIX IMPLEMENTED — FINAL REGRESSION TEST PENDING
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Observed Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> After deleting a selected student, clicking Add displayed a message instructing the user to click Edit instead.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Cause Identified:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">_isEdit</rich_text>
    <rich_text> state was not reset in the deletion handler.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Correction Applied:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Added </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ExitEditMode();</rich_text>
    <rich_text> to the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">finally</rich_text>
    <rich_text> block of </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">btnDelete_Click()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Build Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Successful.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verification Limitation:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Add Mode validation passed after clearing the selection. The behavior immediately following a successful deletion, without using Clear Selection, still requires a separate regression test.

</rich_text>
