    <node unique_id="8" master_id="0" name="14 Test Cases — Round 1 &amp; Round 2" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792157826" ts_lastsave="1792605739">
      <rich_text>
</rich_text>
      <rich_text scale="h1">SchemaX SIS — TEST CASE SHEET v1.0</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Project:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> SchemaX Student Information System
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Team:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> SchemaX
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Test Environment:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> Windows 11, Visual Studio 2026, C# Windows Forms, .NET 10, MySQL
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Testing Round 1:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> October 16, 2026
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Testing Round 2:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> October 17, 2026 — COMPLETED
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Document Updated:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> October 22, 2026


</rich_text>
      <rich_text scale="h2">1. TESTING OBJECTIVE</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
The purpose of this test-case sheet is to verify that the Student Information System performs its intended functions correctly.
Testing focuses on student record management, input validation, database integration, editing, deletion, and searching.
Two rounds of functional testing were conducted to identify problems during initial development and verify corrections after integration.

</rich_text>
      <rich_text scale="h2">2. TEST RESULT LEGEND</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">PASS:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> The feature was tested and behaved as expected.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">FAIL:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> The feature was tested but did not produce the expected result.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">BLOCKED:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> Testing could not be completed because a required feature or integration was unavailable.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">NOT RUN:</rich_text>
      <rich_text> The test had not yet been executed.


</rich_text>
