  <node unique_id="3" master_id="0" name="Setup Guide" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553256" ts_lastsave="1792605920">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">SETUP GUIDE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">1. INTRODUCTION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
This guide explains how to prepare the development environment and open the SchemaX Student Information System project.
The application is developed using C# Windows Forms and MySQL. Visual Studio is used for development, while GitHub is used for version control and collaboration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">2. SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">1. Operating System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Windows 11

• Windows 10 may also be compatible, depending on the installed development tools.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">2. Development Environment</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Visual Studio 2026

◇ .NET 10 SDK

◇ .NET Desktop Development workload


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">3. Database Software</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ MySQL Server

◇ MySQL Workbench


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">4. Version Control</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Git

◇ GitHub account


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">5. Documentation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ CherryTree


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">3. DOWNLOAD THE PROJECT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 1:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open Visual Studio 2026.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 2:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Select "Clone a repository."
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 3:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Enter the GitHub repository URL:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text link="webs https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git">https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 4:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Choose a local folder where the repository will be saved.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 5:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Click "Clone" and wait for the process to finish.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 6:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open the SchemaX.SIS solution in Visual Studio.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Note:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Use the team's designated branch or approved version when testing the project.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">4. OPEN AND BUILD THE APPLICATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 1:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open the SchemaX.SIS solution.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 2:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Wait for Visual Studio to load the project and restore its dependencies.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 3:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check Solution Explorer to confirm that the project files are available.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 4:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Select Build → Build Solution or press Ctrl + Shift + B.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 5:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check the Error List and Output window for any build errors.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 6:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Press F5 to run the application.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The Student Information System window should open if the project builds and starts successfully.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">5. MYSQL DATABASE SETUP</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Name:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">SQL Script Location:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Connection Configuration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS/appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Database Setup Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Install MySQL Server and MySQL Workbench.

2. Start the MySQL80 service.

3. Open MySQL Workbench and connect to the local server.

4. Open and execute </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

5. Verify that the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, and </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text> tables exist.

6. Confirm that the two sample student records can be retrieved.

7. In </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, create </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text> using </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.example.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text> as the template.

8. Configure the local MySQL connection string with the correct database credentials.

9. Keep </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text> excluded from Git.

10. Open the solution in Visual Studio 2026, restore NuGet packages if necessary, build the project, and press F5.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Results:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Local MySQL database successfully created.

• Four required tables verified.

• Two sample student records retrieved in MySQL Workbench.

• Application successfully launched in Visual Studio.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Pending:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Complete application-to-database integration and CRUD verification.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Security Reminder:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Never include actual database passwords in documentation, screenshots, or GitHub commits.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">6. PROJECT FILES AND MODULES</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Form1.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Contains application form logic and event handlers.

◇ Includes current input validation and selection warnings.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Form1.Designer.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Contains the Windows Forms interface components and event connections.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/Validator.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Validates student information and required input formats.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/ExceptionHandler.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Handles exceptions and displays user-friendly error messages.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/ErrorLog.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Records exception information in a local log file.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">logs/errors.txt</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Generated when errors are logged.

◇ Excluded from Git through </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">.gitignore</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database and CRUD Modules</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Awaiting final integration and verification.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">7. BASIC TROUBLESHOOTING</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: The project does not build.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that the required .NET SDK is installed.

◇ Check the Visual Studio Error List.

◇ Restore missing project dependencies.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: The application cannot connect to MySQL.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that the MySQL service is running.

◇ Check the database connection settings.

◇ Verify that the database and required tables exist.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: A validation warning appears.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that required fields are not empty.

◇ Check the Student ID format.

◇ Review the entered student information.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: An unexpected application error occurs.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Read the displayed error message.

◇ Check the generated error log, if available.

◇ Report the issue to the assigned developer.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">Additional Common Problems and Fixes</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: MySQL Workbench cannot connect to the database.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Possible fixes:
• Verify that the MySQL80 service is running.

• Confirm that the username and password are correct.

• Check that MySQL is listening on the configured port (default: 3306).


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: Database tables are missing.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Possible fixes:
◇ Open </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text> in MySQL Workbench.

◇ Execute the SQL script.

◇ Refresh the Schemas panel.

◇ Verify that the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text> database contains four tables.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: Existing students do not appear in the DataGridView.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Current finding:
◇ Student records exist in MySQL, but the form does not load them.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">StudentRepository.GetAll()</rich_text>
    <rich_text> exists but is not called by the current Student Information Form.


Resolution:
◇ Complete the form-to-repository integration.

◇ Retest student loading after the integration changes are merged.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: Add, Edit, or Delete does not update MySQL.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Current finding:
◇ CRUD repository methods exist, but the form's database operations are not fully integrated.


Resolution:
◇ Complete CRUD integration.

◇ Verify the changes in MySQL Workbench.

◇ Record the results in the Testing &amp; Bug Log.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: NuGet dependencies are missing.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Possible fixes:
◇ Open the solution in Visual Studio.

◇ Right-click the solution and select Restore NuGet Packages.

◇ Rebuild the solution and inspect any remaining errors.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: Database credentials might be exposed in Git.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Prevention:
◇ Keep actual credentials only in the local </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

◇ Verify that the file is ignored by Git.

◇ Never upload passwords to GitHub or include them in screenshots.


</rich_text>
