    <rich_text scale="h3">10.1 Latest Application Setup Verification</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The latest integrated project was retrieved from the GitHub develop branch and opened in Visual Studio 2026.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verification Results:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Solution Build: PASS — 2 projects succeeded, 0 failed

• Application Startup: PASS

• MySQL Connection: PASS

• User Registration: PASS

• User Login: PASS

• Dashboard Loading: PASS

• Student Record Retrieval: PASS


These results were verified in the configured local development environment.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">10.2 Updated Database Requirements</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The latest application requires the following five main database tables:
1. students

2. subjects

3. student_subjects

4. attendance

5. users

The users table supports account registration and login.
The students table must also include a user_id column to support account-specific student records.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> The final SQL setup script must be reviewed to confirm that it includes these requirements.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">10.3 Users Table Setup</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
During testing, the application initially displayed:
Table 'schemax_sis.users' doesn't exist.
The local database was missing the table required by UserRepository.cs.
The following structure was used to resolve the issue:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">USE schemax_sis;

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
    user_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    first_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    surname VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    bu_email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    username VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
);</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verification Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS
A test account was successfully registered and authenticated.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">10.4 Student Ownership Schema Update</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The DashboardRepository class requires a user_id column in the students table.
Without this column, the application displayed:
Unknown column 'user_id' in 'where clause'.
For the existing local database, the missing column was added using:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">ALTER TABLE students
ADD COLUMN user_id INT NULL;</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> This statement must only be executed if the column does not already exist.
The two existing student records were then assigned to the registered test account after confirming its user_id.
The actual account ID must be verified before assigning ownership. Do not assume every installation uses user_id = 1.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verification Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">10.5 Database Backup Verification</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Before changing the students table, a backup was created.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Backup Table:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> students_backup_20261022
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Original Student Count:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 2
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Backup Student Count:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 2
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS
The two original student records were preserved.

</rich_text>
