    <rich_text scale="h3">11.1 Student Information Form</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
The Student Information Form successfully opens and displays student records retrieved from the MySQL database.
The interface provides student information fields, a DataGridView, and controls for adding, editing, deleting, searching, filtering, and exporting student records.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.2 Add Student</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open the Student Information Form.

2. Click Clear Selection to return to Add Mode.

3. Enter a valid Student ID.

4. Complete the required student information fields.

5. Click Add.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application validates the information and saves the student record to MySQL.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
A temporary student was successfully added and displayed in the student table.
Required-field, invalid-format, and duplicate Student ID validations were also tested successfully.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.3 Edit Student</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Select an existing student in the DataGridView.

2. Modify the required information.

3. Click Edit to save the changes.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The updated information is saved to MySQL and reflected in the student table.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
An existing student's block was successfully modified and verified in MySQL. The original value was restored after testing.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.4 Delete Student</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Select a student in the DataGridView.

2. Click Delete.

3. Review the confirmation message.

4. Click Yes to confirm or No to cancel.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Confirming deletion removes the selected student from MySQL. Cancelling preserves the record.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Both confirmed deletion and cancellation behavior were successfully tested.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Use temporary test records for future deletion tests. Do not delete original student records.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.5 Search Student Records</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Enter a student name or Student ID in the Search field.

2. Click Search.

3. Review the matching records in the DataGridView.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Search successfully handled full names, partial names, Student IDs, partial IDs, case-insensitive input, and searches with no matching records.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.6 Year Level and Program Filtering</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
The application allows users to filter displayed students by Year Level and Program.
Combined search and filtering were also tested.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Matching records were displayed correctly, and conflicting filter combinations returned zero results.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.7 Clear Search and Clear Selection</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Clear Search:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Resets the Search field, Year Level filter, and Program filter, then restores the full student list.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Clear Selection:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Clears the selected student's information and returns the form to Add Mode.
Both functions produced the expected results during testing.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.8 Export Student Records to CSV</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Display the required student records.

2. Click Export CSV.

3. Select the destination and filename.

4. Save the file.

5. Open the exported CSV in Excel.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Verified Results:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Exporting the complete student list succeeded.

• Exporting filtered student records succeeded.

• Cancelling export did not create an unwanted file.

• Exporting zero search results produced a header-only CSV file.



</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">11.9 Input Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED — PASS
The application successfully displayed validation warnings for the tested invalid inputs, including:
◇ Missing or invalid Student ID

◇ Duplicate Student ID

◇ Missing or invalid student name

◇ Missing or invalid contact number

◇ Missing Program

◇ Missing Gender selection

◇ Missing Year Level selection



