    <rich_text scale="h3">12.7 Exception Handling and Error Logging</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> VERIFIED FOR TESTED SCENARIOS
The application uses the following helper classes:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validator.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Checks student information and required input formats.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">ExceptionHandler.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Displays user-friendly error messages when exceptions are handled.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">ErrorLog.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Records technical exception details in logs/errors.txt.
During October 22 testing, database errors were recorded in the application error log.
The recorded errors included:
◇ Missing users table

◇ Missing user_id column in students


After correcting the local database schema, the application successfully loaded the dashboard.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">12.8 Database Integration Issues Resolved</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Issue 1: Missing Users Table</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The login feature initially failed because the users table was missing.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Resolution:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Created the required table in the local database.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Retest:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Issue 2: Missing Student Ownership Column</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Dashboard statistics initially failed because students did not contain user_id.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Resolution:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Backed up the students table, added the column, and assigned the two existing student records to the registered test account.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Retest:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Issue 3: Database Configuration</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application initially encountered MySQL authentication and configuration errors.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Resolution:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Corrected the local database connection configuration.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Retest:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> PASS

</rich_text>
